---
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import PaginationDemo from '../../components/PaginationDemo';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
---

<Docs title="Pagination" description="Previous, next, numbered pages, and skipped pages for long lists.">
  <h1 class="docs-title">Pagination</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    Previous, next, numbered pages, and skipped pages for long lists. Seven small parts you compose yourself, with plain
    links or router links.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8">
    <PaginationDemo client:load />
  </div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Pagination usage"
      code={`import {
  Pagination,
  PaginationContent,
  PaginationEllipsis,
  PaginationItem,
  PaginationLink,
  PaginationNext,
  PaginationPrevious,
} from "@tulipfarm/sprout/pagination";

<Pagination>
  <PaginationContent>
    <PaginationItem>
      <PaginationPrevious href="?page=1" />
    </PaginationItem>
    <PaginationItem>
      <PaginationLink href="?page=1">1</PaginationLink>
    </PaginationItem>
    <PaginationItem>
      <PaginationLink href="?page=2" isActive>2</PaginationLink>
    </PaginationItem>
    <PaginationItem>
      <PaginationEllipsis />
    </PaginationItem>
    <PaginationItem>
      <PaginationNext href="?page=3" />
    </PaginationItem>
  </PaginationContent>
</Pagination>`}
    />
    <p>
      <code>Pagination</code> is a <code>nav</code> labelled "pagination"; pass
      <code>aria-label</code> to name it, such as "Run history pages".
      <code>PaginationContent</code> is a list and <code>PaginationItem</code> a list item. Which pages to show is your
      choice: the demo keeps the first, last, and nearby pages, and puts <code>PaginationEllipsis</code> in the gaps.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Links, sizes, and labels</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Pagination links"
      code={`<PaginationLink isActive render={<Link to="/inbox?page=2" />}>
  2
</PaginationLink>

<PaginationLink size="icon-sm" href="#">3</PaginationLink>
<PaginationPrevious size="sm" disabled={page === 1} href="#" />
<PaginationNext text="Older" aria-label="Older runs" href="#" />`}
    />
    <p>
      <code>PaginationLink</code> is a Sprõut <code>Button</code> that renders an
      <code>a</code>. It is <code>ghost</code>, and <code>outline</code> with
      <code>aria-current="page"</code> when <code>isActive</code> is set. The Base UI <code>render</code> prop swaps the
      anchor for your router's link.
      <code>size</code> takes any button size: page numbers default to
      <code>icon</code> (32px), and previous and next default to
      <code>default</code>. Pair <code>icon-sm</code> with <code>sm</code> or
      <code>icon-lg</code> with <code>lg</code>. <code>disabled</code> sets
      <code>aria-disabled</code>, removes the link from the tab order, and blocks clicks.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>PaginationPrevious</code> and <code>PaginationNext</code> show a chevron and a <code>text</code> label,
      "Previous" and "Next" by default. Below 640px only the chevron shows. Their names are "Go to previous page" and
      "Go to next page"; pass <code>aria-label</code> when you change the text.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      Links show a focus ring and follow tab order. <code>PaginationEllipsis</code>
      is hidden from screen readers. Pair the control with a status line, such as "Page 3 of 24", so screen readers hear
      the change. Chevrons flip in right-to-left text. Color changes last 120ms and stop when reduced motion is
      requested.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Theme tokens</h2>
    <p>
      Page links use the button's <code>--sprout-muted</code>,<code>--sprout-hover</code>, and{' '}
      <code>--sprout-text</code>. The active page uses <code>--sprout-input</code> and <code>--sprout-surface</code>.
      The ellipsis uses <code>--sprout-muted</code> and the focus ring
      <code>--sprout-focus</code>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
